          "nudge_reason": null,
          "final_text_tail": "\n\nThe task is complete. Changes are in the working tree, confined to `llama-index-core/llama_index/core/base/llms/types.py`:\n\n**What was implemented**\n- New `ImageBlock.get_image_mimetype()` (types.py:85): returns the cached `image_mimetype` if set; otherwise resolves it on demand with the existing `filetype.guess` logic and caches the result on the block (one guess even across repeated calls). It handles both raw bytes (pre-encoding) and the base64 state (post-encoding) by attempting a validating base64 decode first, and returns `None` when it can't be determined.\n- `image_to_base64` (types.py:78-79) no longer contains inline guess logic \u2014 it delegates to `self.get_image_mimetype()`, so construction-time behavior is preserved (the field is still auto-populated for downstream integrations reading `block.image_mimetype`).\n\n**Verification**\n- All 12 existing tests in `tests/base/llms/test_types.py` pass; 25/25 across `tests/base` + `tests/multi_modal_llms`.\n- Sanity-checked: explicit mimetype precedence, guess-at-construction + caching (exactly 1 `filetype.guess` call across constructor + 2 accessor calls), `None` for empty/non-image data, lazy resolution from the already-base64 state, and the legacy pattern of base64-ASCII image bytes.\n\nOne assumption noted: I kept construction-time resolution active (via the new method) rather than removing it, since only `types.py` is modified in the PR and integrations (e.g., the OpenAI LLM package) read `block.image_mimetype` directly.",
